WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.860
- Thank you again for doing my pilot.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:02.693
You did me a solid.

00:00:02.693 --> 00:00:04.130
Nobody ever sees the pilot so you did it

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:05.050
just to be kind.

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:05.883
- No, I, cause I love you.

00:00:05.883 --> 00:00:07.248
- [Kelly] You're nice.

00:00:07.248 --> 00:00:08.081
- I think you're fantastic.

00:00:08.081 --> 00:00:08.914
- [Kelly] Well, I love you too.

00:00:08.914 --> 00:00:09.747
- And it was a year and a half ago?

00:00:09.747 --> 00:00:11.160
- It was a long time ago, yes.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.520
It actually was a very hard interview,

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.710
my very first interview and I told this

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.050
when I ran into you but like,

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.210
your book This Is Me is all about your dad

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.280
and things in your childhood

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.590
and we have very similar childhoods.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.760
My father had died like,

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.940
literally a day before this interview

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.603
and so I was like sitting there.

00:00:24.603 --> 00:00:25.436
- No idea.

00:00:25.436 --> 00:00:27.260
- None of my crew knew so I was literally,

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.550
they were like, we really want you to ask

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.310
and I'm like, I think we're good.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.460
I was like, I think we're good,

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.537
I think we've covered it and I'm like.

00:00:32.537 --> 00:00:35.107
- And we keep these emotions
right here, you and I.

00:00:35.107 --> 00:00:35.940
So...

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.339
- So I was like, let's
just bury it for now

00:00:38.339 --> 00:00:40.220
and then we'll get back to it but no.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.140
Thank you so much.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.230
- It was my pleasure.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.650
- I know you're so busy and it
was a very kind thing to do.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:44.590
- Busy, I'm busy?

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.858
I don't know how you can do what you do.

00:00:45.858 --> 00:00:46.800
- You are busy too, ma'am.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.633
- Well.

00:00:47.633 --> 00:00:48.780
- You are very kind to do my show.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.770
- Busy-ish compared to you, okay.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.660
- Oh no, you're very nice
but what was your worst

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.440
haircut as a child?

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.550
- Well, here's the thing.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.540
It wasn't an accident.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.376
I wanted a rat tail.

00:00:58.376 --> 00:01:01.209
(audience laughs)

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.170
And I got a rat tail folks.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.003
I got a rat tail.

00:01:05.003 --> 00:01:06.620
- Oh my God, it's a rare
statement that you hear

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.210
someone say I wanted a rat tail.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.910
- I was in fourth grade,
it wasn't like last week.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.140
I was in fourth grade and
I was like, this is so cool

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.300
and I could braid it.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.270
Nobody else had a rat tail,

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.720
I was like, I am cutting edge.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.553
- [Kelly] You were.

00:01:17.553 --> 00:01:19.017
- I sure was.

00:01:19.017 --> 00:01:22.090
- Yes, you were country before
country was cool, for sure.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:24.130
- It was like a bowl
cut and it didn't quite,

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.252
it was not cute.

00:01:25.252 --> 00:01:26.170
- I had the bowl, that was my worst.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.550
It was literally, my
mom claims that my hair

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.410
just hadn't grown in, it was
just coming out like that but..

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:31.386
- Nah.

00:01:31.386 --> 00:01:32.289
- It looks like a bowl cut.

00:01:32.289 --> 00:01:33.186
- It was an accident.

00:01:33.186 --> 00:01:34.104
- Yeah, okay mom.

00:01:34.104 --> 00:01:35.000
- Right yeah, and then
I did the whole like,

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.540
have you seen like they shave the head,

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.010
like the back of the head?

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.850
- I've shaved a whole
side before but my sister,

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.440
when I was young in the 80s,
that was really big, right?

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.310
People used to shave the
whole back but keep the top.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:44.440
- Yeah I did that in middle school.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:45.273
- Yeah, my sister did that.

00:01:45.273 --> 00:01:46.356
She's cooler than me.

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:47.189
- I thought it was so cool.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:48.022
- I wasn't that cool.

00:01:48.022 --> 00:01:49.480
- I wasn't either but I pretended.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.850
- So we also have so many similarities

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.950
but you had a ton of jobs, before success.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:55.783
I did as well.

00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:56.710
- Yes.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:57.975
- How many?

00:01:57.975 --> 00:01:59.860
Or what was your most
fun or worst or what?

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.880
- Well I of course, I worked at McDonalds,

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.880
I sold sort of teeth straightening things

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.840
and I was always in the back
drive through at McDonalds

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.910
so every job was about being congenial

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:11.810
and talking to people.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:12.643
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:02:12.643 --> 00:02:15.290
- But gosh, I taught
preschool for five years

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:18.460
and that was so much fun.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:20.100
- I didn't know that's
where you were going.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.170
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.430
- That kind of sounds
like my personal hell.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:27.340
I love children, we have four

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.480
and my mom was a teacher and I used to sit

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.270
on her classes and I vowed
to never be a teacher.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:33.590
- Well 23 of them.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:36.630
- Yes, there's so many of them
and there's only one of you.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:37.870
- Right.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.700
And guys, they're trying to be themselves

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.920
and co-existing with other kids,

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.700
it was really, it was so much fun

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.140
but it was super
challenging, but very fun.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.850
- So have your southern roots helped you

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.730
in this industry at all, you think?

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.920
- I think, you know, I think in the south,

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.260
people treat people kindly

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.220
and I think that kind of
folds over into everything.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.850
You know, how you treat people is really

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.874
the most important thing in life.

00:03:01.874 --> 00:03:02.987
- Yes.

00:03:02.987 --> 00:03:04.320
- But I think also there's southern charm.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.090
I mean, you have it, it just oozes.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:07.630
- Well you have to have it sometimes

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.590
or play the dumb card.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:11.210
- Or when you're like
oh bless their heart.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:12.390
- Yeah, bless your heart

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:13.970
and then you just really
want to talk crap about them.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.319
- You're like...

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:16.221
(audience laughs)

00:03:16.221 --> 00:03:17.860
People that like, cut you off in traffic.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.135
- [Kelly] Bless you.

00:03:19.135 --> 00:03:20.170
- Oh they're probably on
the way to the hospital,

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.818
somethin's really wrong.

00:03:21.818 --> 00:03:23.940
But you know, I just try to,

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.066
my step-daddy who I call
country come to town,

00:03:26.066 --> 00:03:28.210
he would always say really sweet things

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:29.940
that would encourage you and support you

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.898
and he would always say this one phrase.

00:03:31.898 --> 00:03:34.650
It's a sad day when a frog cannot brag

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.500
about his own lily pad.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:37.333
So ...

00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:38.800
- What does that mean, I love it.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:39.790
- Right, right?

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.291
- Cause he doesn't have a lily pad?

00:03:41.291 --> 00:03:42.209
What does that mean?

00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:43.670
- No, it means that you should
be confident in who you are.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:45.021
- Oh I love that.

00:03:45.021 --> 00:03:45.854
- I know, right?

00:03:45.854 --> 00:03:46.907
- I'm stealing it.

00:03:46.907 --> 00:03:48.329
- Yeah so brag about your
own lily pads, y'all.

00:03:48.329 --> 00:03:50.202
- I love my lily pad.

00:03:50.202 --> 00:03:51.194
(audience applause)

00:03:51.194 --> 00:03:52.111
Yes.

00:03:52.111 --> 00:03:52.944
I love that saying, I've
never heard that one.

